\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17a6569-f5a4-507b-8893-5411adb6ea23" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc1900e-1972-56da-a16b-37286f764154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437154} {:answer/id #uuid "17625b3e-b7fb-59c2-9fc5-4405cf2ef025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437156} {:answer/id #uuid "42ce5ab1-0352-5b0f-afd5-6f4b1a84fa3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437162} {:answer/id #uuid "c848c3dc-972f-51a6-bcdf-513299fc05be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437182} {:answer/id #uuid "d291e656-f191-5bd1-8f6c-f229d9c915fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ce5ab1-0352-5b0f-afd5-6f4b1a84fa3b" :answer/type 